#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:5
#: d2d89c0495e94d5697949bb3a54b5bf1
msgid "Understanding Altitude in ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:7
#: c42e2af476da4750a7f9516fd56fc15e
msgid "ArduPilot documentation uses the word \"altitude\" often and in many different ways and contexts. Not all \"altitudes\" mean the same thing, and a good understanding of what altitude means in any given context is important to understand expected operation and behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:14
#: 49cc8af6e6e549fe8af5dd819bb40f6b
msgid "ORIGIN and HOME are set during ground initialization from the GPS and are usually the same location, but the user may move the HOME location during the flight via Mission Planner (for a different RTL point), but the Origin always remains the same unless intentionally reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:18
#: 5cc99755eefc453392215609b83570e3
msgid "Definitions of Altitude (ALT)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:20
#: 27afc51f4b4347d0aff468e2cf7946c5
msgid "In the above diagram, various types of \"altitude\" are shown:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:22
#: dbe549d02ef34fce83e081dba1920faf
msgid "ASL: Altitude above (mean) Sea Level - the altitude of the vehicle expressed as distance above the mean sea level of the world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:23
#: 01c4e3523d64473c94e9d35ba25f1f65
msgid "AGL: Altitude above Ground Level: the altitude of the vehicle above whatever is directly below it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:24
#: 944d31381cef466d837b94ef982c2001
msgid "Relative: Relative altitude above HOME/ORIGIN position's altitude. This is what is displayed in the ground station and OSD as the vehicle's altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:25
#: 73ab099161dc462a8fae1c877e5ab0a2
msgid "Terrain ALT: The height above sea level (asl) of a terrain position. This sometimes, but not always includes, any natural or man-made additions to the terrain's ground altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:26
#: 496262107a7347ee95db20beac5e511b
msgid "Estimated ALT: The autopilot's estimation of vehicle Relative altitude above ORIGIN which is used internally by the vehicle's Altitude Controller to maintain or obtain the Target ALT in altitude controlled modes (Plane: FBWB/AUTO/GUIDED/CRUISE/LOITER/CIRCLE), Copter: ALTHOLD/CIRCLE/LOITER/GUIDED/AUTO/DRIFT)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:27
#: b1f0e48bae1042f4bba6cf01767c17cb
msgid "Target ALT: The desired altitude in altitude controlled modes. Either from pilot input (eg ALTHOLD) or from navigation controller (eg AUTO)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:31
#: a7a04c7132aa4088bcba05f14cc15bca
msgid "Estimated and Target ALT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:38
#: 0cdf22d32c7a46c9b06c6c4737fdea13
msgid "The above simplified diagram shows how altitude control is implemented in ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:40
#: 4300d5c6e96b47238d60003ae6e09540
msgid "The EKF subsystem is responsible for generating attitude, velocity, position, and altitude estimates for the vehicle so that the navigation and control systems can properly operate. EKF takes the IMU, GPS, and BARO sensor inputs and integrates them to provide these estimates, one of which is the Estimated ALT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:42
#: ac3c2c77f8824040915f8388621ebdfb
msgid "This is then fed to the vehicle's altitude control system, which attempts to match the Target ALT in altitude controlled modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:44
#: b1ac99652ac24e7e95b3f892eba15607
msgid "The Target ALT can come from many different sources depending on the vehicle mode. For example, In Plane's FBWB mode, the pitch stick increases or decreases the Target ALT, while in AUTO mode when navigating to a waypoint, the navigation controller feeds a varying ramp of Target ALT as it progresses toward the waypoint to reach that waypoint's new altitude, if different from the previous waypoint's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:46
#: 2b9383aab92743159ab272c16e4e2d00
msgid "In the altitude controller, the Target ALT can also be modified by either Terrain Data from the GCS or SD card if :ref:`TERRAIN_ENABLE<TERRAIN_ENABLE>` is enabled, and/or RangeFinder altitude readings of distance above ground, if enabled and within the range of the rangefinder. Note that in both cases, the displayed altitude in the GCS HUD or OSD is the Estimated Altitude as long as EKF is working (otherwise it will use BARO altitude relative to HOME)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:48
#: efbdbbd21cfb4a968199935c07e18992
msgid "Sometimes the GPS ASL altitude is displayed prior to setting of the Origin position in the EKF during ground initialization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:51
#: 371018a528124e43aaee0ab5b5ed35e1
msgid "Target ALT Modification using RangeFinder (RF)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:54
#: c6c8d75fc6a9408face0e980555dd8dc
msgid "Copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:56
#: b1d718d373fe4384bc7c36f9b3db20ff
msgid "If a downward facing RangeFinder is enabled and within range, then the Target ALT will be modified to use the RF's altitude measurements in Copter and in VTOL modes of Plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:58
#: 7b561708ed524c159f5e12d1c96ebd01
msgid "For example, you are in ALTHOLD in Copter, hovering at 30m and out of the RangeFinder's range. The Target ALT has been set to the current Estimated ALT and will try to hold it. Now you descend using the throttle stick to 10m and are now within the RF's range. When you release the stick, the Target ALT will be set to the RF reported altitude. The Estimated Altitude is still being used to adjust control outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:60
#: 26c2e81755fb4185beecfde566d48878
msgid "If the vehicle is moved over a ground object 1m tall. The Estimated ALT will remain unchanged, since it's based on BARO, GPS ALT, etc. but the Target ALT will be increased by 1M due to the RF readings showing 1m less distance to the ground. Any changes in RF altitude are immediately reflected in the Target ALT, so if the less accurate Estimated ALT erroneously varies a little, the RF effectively immediately cancels that via Target ALT adjustment, yielding more accurate altitude control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:62
#: 0c7581a406624a059172c38c7adce726
msgid "If the RF's measurements change too rapidly (>2m for 3 reports), or the RF moves out of range, then they will be ignored and current altitude from the Estimated ALT set as new Target ALT. This prevents rapid climbs/descents with fast moving RF data. It also means that tracking requiring large,rapid changes, such as quickly approaching a tall object, will result in a possible impact. See :ref:`Object Avoidance <common-object-avoidance-landing-page>` in those cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:64
#: 71e434da2c994f1da421ce3876e16af1
msgid "This is called :ref:`Surface Tracking <copter:terrain-following-manual-modes>` in ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:66
#: a6c648ee23774a559e0fccd2e558747d
msgid "Optionally (normally recommended only for indoor use), the RF can be used as an additional sensor source for the EKF for altitude estimation. This is normally only used when the only altitude sensor available is a RF, since they have very limited range and more subject to environmental impacts to accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:69
#: 49cf6e98a0d54694942440a365ae99a9
msgid "Plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:71
#: d8af9bad0517453a9e750546a5b155c9
msgid "In Plane, when using fixed wing modes, RangeFinder use, when within range and enabled by the :ref:`RNGFND_LANDING<RNGFND_LANDING>` parameter, is limited to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:73
#: 153b26b1c7d341988125d61f00f23646
msgid "Adjusting glide slope during :ref:`Automatic Landings <automatic-landing>`, during the approach and pre-flare phases of the landing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:74
#: 5859c80777db4cf8aca549621a5384c1
msgid "Determining altitude when :ref:`LGR_DEPLOY_ALT<LGR_DEPLOY_ALT>`, or :ref:`LGR_RETRACT_ALT<LGR_RETRACT_ALT>` is reached, if a downward facing RF is active and within range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:75
#: a033e26c89ea4a2680ffa095ce8acb3c
msgid "When :ref:`Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT<Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT>` is reached in VTOL landings in QuadPlane, if a downward facing RF is active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:76
#: 9bbae0f65a244dfcba35be36d45f5571
msgid "Determining if below :ref:`Q_ASSIST_ALT<Q_ASSIST_ALT>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:77
#: 60c90f732a5d4d579b7b64c8ff94e244
msgid "Determining if below :ref:`Q_VFWD_ALT<Q_VFWD_ALT>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:80
#: 5896e9b351dd4a9bb58947c8e352051f
msgid "Target ALT Modification using Terrain Following Data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:82
#: e43fa396ccd6439681996decf4816e5c
msgid "If Terrain Following is enabled and active, then the terrain altitude changes are used to increase or decrease the Target ALT for whatever the present location is, as it moves, depending on vehicle and mode. For details see :ref:`common-terrain-following` for Plane or :ref:`terrain-following` for Copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-understanding-altitude.rst:84
#: 4cd90acb5ca74c959292d5a249ac0966
msgid "For Copter, this can be combined with RangeFinder use for obtain :ref:`Surface Tracking<terrain-following-manual-modes>` over obstacles at low altitudes."
msgstr ""
